FINDINGS:
1. [MINOR] src/stdlib.rs:1415 — the user-visible `length` signature still reads `length(text) -> number of bytes` and lists only text/list, so it both contradicts the real character-count behaviour (`tests/test_text.rb:76-97` pins characters, not bytes) and omits the deque case this phase adds (`src/runtime.rs:2556-2596`). REPL/introspection help therefore documents a surface the language does not have and hides the one it gained. Fix: update the entry to `length(text) -> number of characters`, `length(list) -> number of items`, and `length(deque) -> number of items`. VERIFIED: read the table at `src/stdlib.rs:1414-1417` and the supporting tests/spec.
2. [STYLE] src/runtime.rs:2519 — `deque_length` re-sums each spine tree with `stack_tree_budget` even though `deque_parts` (called on the previous line) already summed every tree and enforced `MAX_DEQUE_ITEMS` at `src/runtime.rs:2029-2044`. The duplicated budget arithmetic is harmless today only because the call ordering guarantees validation; a future change to either loop can silently desynchronise the cap. Fix: have `deque_parts` return the validated total, or extract one helper both paths use.

